<?php

return [
    ['A patient with chronic myeloid leukemia is monitored after treatment; the laboratory performs the BCR-ABL1 fusion analysis on peripheral blood.', 'The BCR-ABL1 fusion transcript in CML is detected and quantitated by which technique to track the molecular response?', 'intermediate', 'C', 'Chromosome banding only', 'A serology assay', 'Reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction (RT-qPCR) targeting the fusion mRNA, combined with the chromosome analysis for the Philadelphia chromosome', 'An ELISA', 'The BCR-ABL fusion is identified by the RT-qPCR on the transcripts (with the p210 and p190 variants) and confirmed by the conventional karyotype or the FISH for the Philadelphia chromosome; the quantitative PCR follows the molecular response on the international scale during the tyrosine kinase inhibitor therapy. The karyotype alone cannot detect the minimal residual disease.'],
    ['A prenatal sample is referred for aneuploidy testing; the laboratory uses a rapid method on the amniotic fluid.', 'The most rapid method for confirming a common trisomy on the cultured amniocytes or the amniotic fluid sample is which technique?', 'easy', 'A', 'Fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) with the chromosome-specific probes', 'A urine culture', 'A hemagglutination assay', 'A glucose tolerance test', 'FISH with the alpha-satellite probes for chromosomes 13, 18, 21, X, and Y gives the rapid same-day result for the common aneuploidies, with the karyotype confirming and the details added in the full chromosome analysis; the interphase cells can be scored directly without the culture. The culture-based karyotype is slower and the other assays are unrelated.'],
    ['A blood sample for a microdeletion syndrome is analyzed; the laboratory method is explained to the genetic counselor.', 'The detection of a genomic copy number change that a single-gene test would miss (such as a chromosome 22q11 microdeletion) is best achieved by which approach?', 'intermediate', 'D', 'A single PCR primer pair', 'A glucose assay', 'A serology', 'Chromosomal microarray (or FISH with the locus-specific probe) that surveys the copy number across the genome', 'The 22q11.2 (DiGeorge) deletion and the other microdeletions are submicroscopic, so the chromosome microarray with the array-CGH or SNP genotyping detects the copy-number change while the routine karyotype and the single-gene PCR miss it; FISH with the locus-specific probe confirms the specific deletion. The microarray therefore covers the whole genome at the copy-number level.'],
    ['A hematologic malignancy is classified by the expression of an AML-specific fusion; the molecular laboratory tests the bone marrow.', 'The RUNX1-RUNX1T1 and PML-RARA fusions in acute myeloid and promyelocytic leukemia are detected by which technique, and for the PML-RARA the result is essential for which reason?', 'advanced', 'B', 'A glucose tolerance test', 'RT-PCR for the fusion mRNA (and FISH or karyotype), with the PML-RARA required to start the differentiation therapy with the retinoic acid', 'A screening immunoassay', 'A urine examination', 'The fusion transcripts characterize AML subtypes and the PML-RARA of the M3 promyelocytic leukemia, where targeted retinoic acid and arsenic therapy are life-saving, so the molecular detection and the MRD tracking use the RT-qPCR (with the transcript types distinguished) and the FISH; the cytogenetic confirmation of the t(15;17) is the companion. The detection directly governs the treatment in the promyelocytic case.'],
    ['A solid tumor biopsy is analyzed for a targeted therapy; the laboratory evaluates the epidermal growth factor receptor mutation status.', 'An EGFR mutation in non-small cell lung cancer is most commonly detected by which molecular approach?', 'intermediate', 'C', 'A karyotype', 'An ABO type', 'Amplicon or next-generation sequencing of the EGFR gene (with the common exon 19 deletions and the L858R point mutation) using the tumor tissue or the plasma cell-free DNA', 'A latex agglutination', 'EGFR testing uses targeted PCR and Sanger or NGS panels that detect the sensitizing exon 19 deletions and the L858R mutation and the T790M resistance mutation in the tissue or the circulating DNA; the result predicts the response to the tyrosine kinase inhibitors. Karyotype and serology have no role in the mutation detection.'],
    ['A patient with a suspected hereditary disorder is tested; the laboratory runs a multigene panel and identifies a pathogenic variant.', 'The variant classification in a diagnostic molecular laboratory follows which standard?', 'intermediate', 'A', 'The American College of Medical Genetics guidelines dividing the variants into the pathogenic, likely pathogenic, uncertain significance, likely benign, and benign categories', 'A local arbitrary number', 'A vendor confidence', 'A single-gene opinion', 'The American College of Medical Genetics and Genomics and the Association for Molecular Pathology framework classifies the sequence variants into the five categories (pathogenic, likely pathogenic, uncertain significance, likely benign, benign) using the population, the functional, the segregation, and the in silico evidence; the report states the variant and the classification and the laboratory notes the clinical interpretation. The formal classification protects the clinical decisions.'],
    ['A molecular laboratory monitors the minimal residual disease in an acute lymphoblastic leukemia patient after induction.', 'The immunoglobulin and T-cell receptor gene rearrangements are used to track the residual disease in ALL by which method?', 'advanced', 'D', 'A karyotype', 'A FISH probe only', 'A glucose assay', 'Real-time PCR (or the high-throughput sequencing) of the clone-specific immunoglobulin or T-cell receptor rearrangement junction sequences', 'The clonal Ig/TCR rearrangements give an individual patient specific junction sequence that the allele-specific real-time PCR and the deep sequencing follow over the treatment course; the MRD threshold predicts the relapse and guides the therapy intensity. The karyotype and the FISH do not reach the sensitivity of the junction-tracking PCR.'],
    ['A prenatal carrier screening panel includes the cystic fibrosis gene testing; the result is reported with the classification.', 'A common CFTR variant such as the delta F508 is detected by which method, and the limitation of the panel (the residual risk) is explained how?', 'intermediate', 'B', 'A serology', 'A multiplexed PCR or genotyping that detects the panel of the common mutations, with the residual risk reported because the panel does not cover all possible variants', 'A urine screening', 'A white cell count', 'CFTR carrier screening detects a defined panel of the common pathogenic variants by PCR-based genotyping or sequencing, and because the panel and the sequencing capture only the screened regions, the residual carrier risk after a negative result is reported and adjusted by the ethnicity; the delta F508 is the most common variant in the northern European groups. The residual risk depends on the coverage of the panel.'],
    ['A molecular laboratory validates a viral load assay for HIV monitoring; the report includes the log change.', 'The interpretation of the HIV-1 viral load during therapy relies on which characteristic of the assay?', 'intermediate', 'C', 'A visual inspection', 'A threshold of positivity only', 'The lower limit of quantitation and the precision, so a 10-fold (1 log) change is a genuine treatment response rather than an analytic variation', 'The color', 'The clinical interpretation of the HIV load during antiretroviral therapy uses the assay lower limit (e.g., 20-40 copies/mL) and the reproducibility, because the goal is full suppression below the limit and the meaningful change is a log-fold trend; the viral genotype and the resistance additionally inform the choice. The accuracy at the low end and the precision define the suppressibility.'],
    ['A tumor is tested for the HER2 copy number by FISH in a breast cancer sample; the result is scored.', 'The HER2 gene amplification by FISH is scored and interpreted using the ratio of which signals?', 'intermediate', 'A', 'The HER2 (chromosome 17) signals normalized to the centromere 17 (CEP17) probe, with a ratio greater than the guideline threshold indicating a positive result', 'The estrogen receptor only', 'The Ki67 fraction', 'The tumor size', 'The FISH result for HER2 is the HER2-to-CEP17 signal ratio (and the average HER2 copy number) per the ASCO-CAP guidelines: a ratio greater than 2.0 (or an average copy number above 6) is amplified, guiding the anti-HER2 therapy; the ER and the proliferation markers address different therapeutic decisions. The ratio and the copy number, not the absolute fluorescence, determine the amplification.'],

];